IF @mode != "publish"
    RETURN "Estimate publication was not selected."

DO Verify @request explicitly requests publication and @saved_estimate is
    complete, placeholder-free, and supported. Require six rows in order,
    nonnegative integer team scores, explained zeros, categorized reasons and
    uncertainty, no double-counting, the correct six-score total, and a
    supported numeric Final Estimate ending in SP. Do not rewrite missing or
    invalid content.

DO Resolve the private absolute acli and ix executables under shared Inux
    guidance. Report missing tools without setup, login, or version probes.
    Return an object with acli and ix. AS tools

RUN @tools.acli jira workitem comment list --key @ticket_id --json --paginate AS comments_result

DO Parse @comments_result.stdout as JSON. Check for duplicate estimate comments
    and material clarifications. Return an object with
    evidence_contradicts_draft, identical_comment, and duplicate_url. Never
    replace unrelated comments. AS comment_state

IF @comment_state.evidence_contradicts_draft == TRUE
    ASK "Jira evidence contradicts the saved estimate. Type yes to revise it later, or no to leave it unchanged." AS revision_request

    DO Normalize @revision_request to lowercase "yes" or "no"; return "invalid"
        for every other answer. AS revision_choice

    IF @revision_choice == "yes"
        RETURN "Publication stopped. Run /inux estimate improve with the new evidence; the saved estimate is unchanged."

    IF @revision_choice == "no"
        RETURN "Publication stopped because evidence contradicts the draft; the saved estimate is unchanged."

    RETURN "Publication stopped because the answer was not exactly yes or no; the saved estimate is unchanged."

IF @comment_state.identical_comment == FALSE
    USE ../../references/cli.md AS cli_guidance

    DO Publish @saved_estimate as one bounded transaction. Follow @cli_guidance.
        Create one unique private temporary directory and ADF path. Run @tools.ix
        with the separate arguments adf, @estimate_path, and that path; verify the
        ADF faithfully represents @saved_estimate. Immediately re-read the active
        ticket ID and saved estimate, and do not publish if either differs from
        @ticket_id or @saved_estimate. Then run @tools.acli with the separate
        arguments jira, workitem, comment, create, --key, @ticket_id, --body-file,
        the ADF path, and --json. Parse and verify the comment or ticket URL,
        looking it up only when absent. Remove only the unique temporary directory
        before completing or failing. Return the verified URL. AS publication_url
ELSE
    SET publication_url = @comment_state.duplicate_url

PRINT Report @ticket_id, the saved SP, @estimate_path, @publication_url, assumptions, unrelated gaps, and justified SP changes briefly.
